\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesus calls us! O'er the tumult
\par Of our life's wild restless sea,
\par Day by day His sweet voice soundeth,
\par Saying: Christian, follow Me-
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. As, of old, apostles heard it
\par By the Galilean lake,
\par Turned from home and toil and kindred,
\par Leaving all for His dear sake.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Jesus calls us from the worship
\par Of the vain world's golden store,
\par From each idol that would keep us,
\par Saying: Christian, love Me more!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. In our joys and in our sorrows,
\par Days of toil and hours of ease,
\par Still He calls, in cares and pleasures,
\par That we love Him more than these.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Jesus calls us! By Thy mercies,
\par Saviour, make us hear Thy call,
\par Give our hearts to Thine obedience,
\par Serve and love Thee best of all.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

